-- title:
--   Lemma 7.2 — tightness for a history-measurable terminal query
-- statement:
--   In the standing AMP setup at fixed horizon $T$, let $z_d\in H_{n(d)}$ be any sequence of queries measurable for the actual alternating-observation history $\mathcal F_{d,T}$. There exists a measurable family $C_{d,T}$ such that almost surely
--
--   $$\|A_dz_d\|_{\rm op}\le C_{d,T}\|z_d\|_n,\qquad
--   \lim_{L\to\infty}\limsup_{d\to\infty}\mathbb P(C_{d,T}>L)=0.$$
--
--   The family is chosen after the query sequence and may depend on it. This supplies a dimension-independent tight factor for each history-measurable query sequence. It is not a single random bound simultaneously for all queries. At $z_d=0$ both sides of the inequality are zero. No numerical rate is asserted.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: positive matrix dimension d tends to infinity → natural index j represents physical dimension j+1; reason: bijection with all positive dimensions; n(j) remains arbitrary
--   - encoding: the recursively specified Gaussian–semicircular limiting process → arbitrary probability/C*-space realizations satisfying precisely the state law; reason: finite Gaussian covariance and semicircular Fock realizations exist and have identical moments and faithful norms
--   - encoding: upper-tail tightness of a family that can be chosen nonnegative → absolute-tail tightness of the chosen family; reason: a nonnegative tight family can always be chosen; the requested existential bound is unchanged
--   - generalization: the terminal-query application with fixed T ≥ 1 → also permits the empty observation history T = 0; reason: F_0 is generated by the independent initialization, so the fresh conditional GOE law gives tightness at T = 0; all positive source horizons remain included
--   - encoding: sample sizes n(d) with n(d) → ∞ → n(d) ≥ 1 for every d; reason: nondegeneracy only; at n = 0 the source's 1/n and n^{-1/2} normalizations are undefined, and n(d) → ∞ leaves only finitely many such d, which no limit statement sees
-- source:
--   August Chen, Ahmed El Alaoui, STOC 2027 submission #1182 (October 2026), pp. 37–38, Lemma 7.2

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FreeProbAMP_StateEvolution_History

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter
open scoped BigOperators Topology NNReal Matrix
set_option autoImplicit false
noncomputable section

namespace FreeProbAMP.StateEvolution

/-- Lemma 7.2, submission pp.37–38. The bound is per query sequence. -/
theorem terminal_query_tightness
    {Ω E B : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] [MeasurableSpace E] [CStarAlgebra B]
    (D : FiniteData Ω) (L : LimitData E B) (T : ℕ) (α : ℝ)
    (hA : AMPAssumptions D L T α) (hL : StateLaw L T α D.a D.g)
    (z : (d : ℕ) → Ω → Fin (D.n d) → ℝ)
    (hz : ∀ d, Measurable[(D.observations d).F T] (z d)) :
    ∃ C : ℕ → Ω → ℝ, (∀ d, Measurable (C d)) ∧
      (∀ d, ∀ᵐ ω ∂D.μ, opNorm (applyA (D.A d ω) (z d ω)) ≤ C d ω * vecNorm (z d ω)) ∧
      Tight D.μ C := by sorry

end FreeProbAMP.StateEvolution
